{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789917966,"nonce":"bR2ilHNrMZ0IWhNJtuWq1ka1RnA=","title":"Lua: a function declared into a table has parameters typed nil","message":"`function M.check(x) if x then return 'yes' else return 'no' end end` printed 'no' for M.check(1), and `function M.eq(a, b) return a == b end` was true for M.eq(1, 2). A dotted-name declaration was neither a known function (no direct calls feed its parameters) nor marked escaping, so its parameters settled to Nil and the lowering folded truth tests and comparisons on them. The function is a value in a table: it escapes.","files":null}]}